.TH @APP@ 1 "@DATE@" "odox @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@APP@ \- @SUMMARY@
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @APP@
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
@DESCRIPTION@
.PP
The document is read from the file and nothing is sent anywhere. Nothing is
written either: this release reads OpenDocument and does not save it.
.SH OPTIONS
There are none. A path given on the command line is opened at startup; a
document may also be dropped on the window or chosen with Ctrl+O.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open a document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+R
Read the open document from disk again.
.TP
.B Ctrl+W
Close it.
.TP
.B Ctrl+plus, Ctrl+minus, Ctrl+0
Zoom in, zoom out, and back to actual size.
.SH FILES
None. @APP@ writes no configuration, no cache and no temporary copy.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xodt (1),
.BR xods (1),
.BR xodp (1)
.PP
Each reads one kind of OpenDocument file and names its sibling when handed
another.
.SH AUTHOR
David M. Anderson.
